1
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:12,160
Aunt Liu, where is my dad?

2
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:14,240
Your dad is dead.

3
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:16,920
<i>I lost both of my sons.</i>

4
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,800
Do you have any idea how much I lost?

5
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:21,880
<i>I don't agree with this at all.</i>

6
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:24,400
Bringing a poisonous snake
this close to us?

7
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:26,280
One day, it's going to bite.

8
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:29,520
Why didn't you ask for ten or 20 million?

9
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:32,520
You already stole so much money
and jewelry from them.

10
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:33,840
‎PREVIOUSLY

11
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:36,840
<i>You're about to learn
that a construction worker's life</i>

12
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:38,560
<i>isn't as easy as you think.</i>

13
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:46,200
I haven't held 500,000 baht in ages.

14
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:47,520
My hands are shaking.

15
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:13,080
Don't you dare, or I'll--

16
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:14,800
Mom!

17
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:16,200
Yeah, it's me.

18
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:19,160
Why are you following me?

19
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:22,360
I'm afraid you'll take the money
Hathaya sent and gamble it away.

20
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:27,400
- You know about that?
- I'm not stupid.

21
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:30,320
I heard everything.
I know what's going on.

22
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:33,640
Give me the money.
I'll pay them back myself.

23
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:37,640
Mom, I'm the one who borrowed from them.

24
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:40,520
I have to take responsibility.
I'll pay them back myself.

25
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:42,000
Then I'm coming with you.

26
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:46,120
Come on, Mom. I've learned my lesson too.

27
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:49,440
I'm terrified those guys
will gut me alive.

28
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:51,960
You don't have to come.
I'll pay them back myself.

29
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:53,760
If you're determined to pay them back,

30
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:55,760
then I'm determined to go with you.

31
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:59,920
Fine, fine. If you don't trust me,

32
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,200
then come with me. Come on.

33
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:05,360
Motorcycle! Stop!

34
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:07,400
I'm going, Mom.

35
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:09,120
- Hey!
- Go.

36
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:11,760
- Go!
- Wait for me, Hathai!

37
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:14,120
Hathai, please!

38
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:16,680
Please

39
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:19,760
don't let Hathai go gambling again.

40
00:05:20,280 --> 00:05:21,840
Please.

41
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:24,000
For goodness' sake!

42
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,920
Come. You can get down now.

43
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:46,560
What are you laughing at?

44
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:49,480
Look at you. You look like a madwoman.

45
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:52,760
Come on. Get down.

46
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:54,480
Hurry.

47
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:00,600
I'm definitely going to help Grandpa.

48
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:07,840
Wait. Come here. Where are you going?

49
00:06:07,920 --> 00:06:09,440
To the office.

50
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:10,840
No.

51
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:13,720
Your workplace is over there.

52
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:24,960
You want me to do construction work?

53
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:26,520
Yes.

54
00:06:27,760 --> 00:06:30,720
And remember the most important rule.

55
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:33,920
You're working here as a laborer.

56
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,440
If you tell anyone that you're
Mr. Pichai's granddaughter,

57
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:39,320
the agreement you made with him

58
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:41,280
becomes null and void.

59
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:55,600
Everyone! Gather over here!

60
00:06:58,080 --> 00:06:59,400
Come on!

61
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:04,400
The boss brought us a new worker today.

62
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:06,360
Hello. My name is Hathaya.

63
00:07:06,440 --> 00:07:08,600
Hello. I'm Max.

64
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:09,520
Pleasure.

65
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:11,480
- Nice to meet you.
- Alright.

66
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:13,320
I work under Ramil.

67
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:15,960
I see.

68
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:17,520
All right, everyone.

69
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:21,040
This is our new worker. She starts today.

70
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:24,160
- Hello. My name is Hathaya--
- All right, go!

71
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:27,200
Back to work. Get it done. Go team!

72
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:32,920
Get moving.

73
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:34,880
Come on! Hurry!

74
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:37,040
Keep it moving!

75
00:07:37,680 --> 00:07:40,000
I didn't even get to introduce myself.

76
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:41,120
Why?

77
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:44,080
Will knowing their full names
and home addresses

78
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:46,000
make the work get done faster?

79
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:48,160
You have no manners.

80
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:52,240
Go work. Carry that cement
over there and plaster the building.

81
00:07:52,320 --> 00:07:53,800
I've never done it before.

82
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:01,560
Go over there.

83
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:03,960
Go.

84
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:06,560
Wait. Take two.

85
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:08,640
Hurry up. No slacking.

86
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:24,040
Think she can handle it?

87
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:27,160
She has to.

88
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:30,080
No slacking on this job.

89
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:32,400
Nice.

90
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:36,920
- Still?
- What do you mean, still?

91
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:39,560
You're still here? I said no slacking.

92
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:42,040
- Go! Yeah, you!
- Me?

93
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:44,320
- No slacking.
- Is that the right way?

94
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:47,280
No slacking! No slacking!

95
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:53,960
Let's see how long

96
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:57,160
this pampered rich girl lasts.

97
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:01,840
Having you around really saves me money.

98
00:10:01,920 --> 00:10:03,680
I don't even have to go to the nail salon.

99
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:06,920
- Be gentle!
- Yes, ma'am.

100
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,440
Madam. You get your nails done

101
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:13,200
about twice a week.

102
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:16,920
Over a whole year,

103
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:20,960
I must save you thousands,
maybe even tens of thousands of baht.

104
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:23,520
Don't start holding it over my head.

105
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:25,680
I never make anyone work for free.

106
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:44,840
Twenty baht?

107
00:10:44,920 --> 00:10:48,080
Madam, my heart is so full.

108
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:50,000
A whole 20 baht!

109
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:53,120
Go on. Get out of here.

110
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:56,880
Just looking at your face
makes my heart sink.

111
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:57,880
Yes, ma'am.

112
00:10:58,600 --> 00:11:00,360
Mine is very, very full.

113
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:01,960
My heart is overflowing.

114
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:04,360
- Twenty baht?
- Go.

115
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:07,080
Yes, ma'am.

116
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:09,560
Where's Hathaya?

117
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:12,640
I haven't seen her at all this morning.

118
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:16,520
Grandpa sent her to work
at the construction site.

119
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:19,880
I love it. By now,
she's probably passed out

120
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:22,720
face-first into a tub of cement.

121
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:25,720
Working around construction workers?

122
00:11:25,800 --> 00:11:28,120
A few days and she'll probably
end up with a husband.

123
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:32,440
- By the way, who came to pick her up?
- That lunatic Ramil.

124
00:11:33,480 --> 00:11:34,640
Ramil?

125
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:36,600
You still miss him?

126
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:38,480
Mom.

127
00:11:38,560 --> 00:11:42,400
Someone like me would never
lower myself to be with someone like him.

128
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:45,080
A parasite like him

129
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:47,840
belongs with that parasite Hathaya.

130
00:11:47,920 --> 00:11:49,880
Then they can have
a whole family of parasites.

131
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:55,440
Where do you come up with this stuff?
You're hilarious.

132
00:11:55,520 --> 00:11:56,760
Family of parasites?

133
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:01,600
You're hilarious.

134
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:05,840
It's noon, everyone! Take a break!

135
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:07,160
Come on!

136
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:09,280
Go eat!

137
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:11,800
Come on.

138
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:16,360
Let's go.

139
00:12:17,760 --> 00:12:20,640
- Where are you going?
- To eat.

140
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:23,320
I didn't bring any food.
There should be a food stall nearby.

141
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:25,720
- You can't go. Your work isn't done.
- Huh?

142
00:12:25,800 --> 00:12:27,960
But I already poured
all that cement for you.

143
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:31,520
And you're going to let the cement dry
onto the buckets? Wash them first.

144
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:33,760
I'll help her. It'll get done faster.

145
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:36,560
- No.
- I just want to help.

146
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:38,440
I said no.

147
00:12:40,520 --> 00:12:41,360
Okay!

148
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:43,200
No, no, no.

149
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:45,760
Hang in there. I'm starving!

150
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:53,440
Go wash the cement buckets.
And make sure they're completely clean.

151
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:56,680
If I see even a trace
of cement left on them,

152
00:12:57,640 --> 00:12:58,880
you don't get to eat.

153
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:02,760
Go.

154
00:13:21,080 --> 00:13:22,160
Thanks.

155
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:30,040
Come to think of it,

156
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:32,920
that new worker looks really familiar.

157
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,760
I swear I've seen her somewhere before.

158
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,600
She's Mr. Pichai's granddaughter.

159
00:13:40,040 --> 00:13:41,160
His granddaughter?

160
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:52,080
Then why are you making her work
out here in the sun and wind?

161
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:56,560
Remember that story people used to tell?

162
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:58,240
The eldest daughter-in-law

163
00:13:58,320 --> 00:14:02,160
was caught having an affair, then
ran away with her daughter and the money.

164
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:04,200
And because of that,
both his sons ended up dead.

165
00:14:04,920 --> 00:14:06,040
That granddaughter?

166
00:14:06,640 --> 00:14:09,320
She disappeared for more than ten years,
then suddenly came back.

167
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:13,240
So Mr. Pichai is convinced
she came back for the inheritance.

168
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:17,880
Still, that doesn't seem fair.

169
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:20,720
Her mother might have been unfaithful,

170
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:23,240
but you can't blame her
for her mother's actions.

171
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:28,800
I hate to judge people like that too.

172
00:14:30,400 --> 00:14:32,520
But what can I do? I was given orders.

173
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:38,560
And don't tell anyone about this.
Understand?

174
00:14:39,160 --> 00:14:41,720
I promise. My lips are sealed.

175
00:15:17,560 --> 00:15:21,400
I've got 500,000.
If I can make another 500,000,

176
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:26,760
I'll have enough money
to pay for Mom's treatment.

177
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:32,480
Hathaya, you won't have to keep working
until the end of the month anymore.

178
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:41,440
Hi.

179
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:55,880
Damn it, Aow. He forgot his bag again.

180
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:01,360
Boss, who are you looking for?

181
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:04,319
Where is she?

182
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:08,839
She? Who?

183
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:12,359
Good one? Bad one?

184
00:17:19,319 --> 00:17:20,680
Why'd you hit me?

185
00:17:21,319 --> 00:17:23,920
She probably went to get something to eat.

186
00:17:28,280 --> 00:17:29,760
Break time is over.

187
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:33,640
Is she trying to slack off and test me?

188
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:38,960
I have a card! I have a card!

189
00:17:39,040 --> 00:17:42,000
- Without ID, you're going to jail.
- I'm not going.

190
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:44,600
- You're coming with us.
- What are you doing?

191
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:46,680
What's going on?

192
00:17:46,760 --> 00:17:48,840
None of your business. Stay out of it.

193
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:52,240
He's my friend. We work at the same place.

194
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,640
So you're a migrant worker too?

195
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:58,680
Your Thai is pretty good.
I bet you don't have an ID either.

196
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:00,520
Want to come to the station?

197
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:08,560
If you don't want to go to jail,

198
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:13,120
sleep with me, and I'll let you go.

199
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:16,080
I'm Thai.

200
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:18,200
You should've said so.

201
00:18:19,120 --> 00:18:21,160
Go back to work. Stay out of this.

202
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:24,200
I already told you. He's my friend.

203
00:18:24,280 --> 00:18:25,760
What are you arresting him for?

204
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:28,120
He's a migrant worker without his ID card.

205
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:30,200
My card is at the construction site.

206
00:18:30,280 --> 00:18:32,000
I said I'd go back and get it,

207
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:33,720
but they won't let me.

208
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:37,520
No ID means he broke the law.
He has to pay a fine.

209
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:40,120
I don't have money to pay.

210
00:18:40,200 --> 00:18:41,600
He said if I give him my gold chain,

211
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:44,240
I won't have to go to jail.

212
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:45,840
How can you do that?

213
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:48,400
Do what? I'm just enforcing the law.

214
00:18:48,480 --> 00:18:50,240
If you're really enforcing the law,

215
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:53,840
then you should take him to the station
and have his employer pay the fine.

216
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:56,720
Instead, you threatened him
and tried to take his gold chain.

217
00:18:57,240 --> 00:18:59,400
Are you a police officer or a thief?

218
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:02,040
Talking to me like that is an insult.

219
00:19:02,120 --> 00:19:03,600
I'll make sure you're prosecuted.

220
00:19:03,680 --> 00:19:06,800
And what about when you
called me a migrant worker

221
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:09,800
and told me to sleep with you
in exchange for letting me go?

222
00:19:09,880 --> 00:19:11,200
Is that legal?

223
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:17,440
I recorded everything.

224
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:19,920
And I'll make sure
you're held accountable too.

225
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,680
Wait, wait.

226
00:19:22,480 --> 00:19:25,360
Calm down. You're Thai just like us.

227
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:27,440
I'll apologize on behalf of him.

228
00:19:27,520 --> 00:19:28,840
No ID. Still illegal.

229
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:31,160
Strictly speaking, yes.

230
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:33,800
He was wrong not to carry his ID card.

231
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:37,040
But as one human being to another,

232
00:19:37,560 --> 00:19:40,320
you could let him go back to the site
and bring the it to you.

233
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:41,920
It wouldn't take that much time.

234
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,880
You say you're enforcing the law,

235
00:19:43,960 --> 00:19:45,840
but you're breaking it yourself.

236
00:19:46,440 --> 00:19:47,920
Why do you even care?

237
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,720
He's just a migrant worker.

238
00:19:50,880 --> 00:19:53,760
You have no right to point
at anyone and call them a parasite.

239
00:19:53,840 --> 00:19:56,280
He came here to work legally.

240
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:59,840
You know perfectly well that many
Thai people don't want to do manual labor

241
00:19:59,920 --> 00:20:01,720
unless the wages are high.

242
00:20:01,800 --> 00:20:04,960
You should be thanking them
for coming here and helping us.

243
00:20:05,640 --> 00:20:07,280
And if anyone is a parasite

244
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:09,280
like you say,

245
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:11,320
it's people like you.

246
00:20:11,400 --> 00:20:13,880
You're the parasites of the police force.

247
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:14,960
I'll slap your mouth!

248
00:20:16,360 --> 00:20:17,560
Why are you getting involved?

249
00:20:18,200 --> 00:20:19,680
I'm their boss.

250
00:20:22,080 --> 00:20:24,120
Here are their cards.

251
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:27,880
They work for Mr. Pichai.

252
00:20:28,480 --> 00:20:30,600
Mr. Pichai? The owner
of the big development project?

253
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:32,640
You know Mr. Pichai

254
00:20:32,720 --> 00:20:34,400
never employs illegal workers.

255
00:20:35,440 --> 00:20:38,160
He also supports activities
at your police station.

256
00:20:38,920 --> 00:20:41,200
If you keep acting
outside the law like this,

257
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:44,120
I may have to call your superior.

258
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:47,680
Come on. It was just a misunderstanding.

259
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:50,120
Carry your card with you next time.

260
00:20:53,360 --> 00:20:54,840
I apologize for my friend.

261
00:20:55,360 --> 00:20:57,560
It won't happen again.

262
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:05,720
Thank you so much, boss.

263
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:08,240
If you hadn't helped me,
I would've been in trouble.

264
00:21:08,320 --> 00:21:11,120
Thank you. Thank you so much.

265
00:21:11,880 --> 00:21:14,640
It's okay. We should help each other.

266
00:21:14,720 --> 00:21:16,720
Make sure you carry
your ID with you from now.

267
00:21:17,280 --> 00:21:18,960
And save up your money

268
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:21,080
so you can go home.
Your parents are waiting.

269
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:25,000
Thank you. Thank you so much.

270
00:22:04,320 --> 00:22:05,240
Hey.

271
00:22:06,640 --> 00:22:09,320
Next time, don't act so tough
and reckless like that. It's dangerous.

272
00:22:09,960 --> 00:22:12,480
I'm not scared. I have my phone.

273
00:22:15,240 --> 00:22:16,960
Give me my phone back.

274
00:22:19,160 --> 00:22:22,240
You can't even protect one little phone.

275
00:22:22,320 --> 00:22:23,400
Here.

276
00:22:24,720 --> 00:22:27,800
Corrupt people like that can use their
authority and physical force against you.

277
00:22:28,360 --> 00:22:31,120
Think before you do something.

278
00:22:31,880 --> 00:22:33,520
Make sure you can protect yourself first.

279
00:22:34,240 --> 00:22:36,280
I can't stand watching
people get taken advantage of.

280
00:22:37,320 --> 00:22:40,160
When I lived in Ranong,
I knew a lot of people like them.

281
00:22:40,240 --> 00:22:42,760
They have to cross borders
and travel so far

282
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:45,520
just to work here and earn money
for their parents and families.

283
00:22:46,480 --> 00:22:49,240
They struggle for every single baht.

284
00:22:49,320 --> 00:22:51,280
They endure exhaustion
and all kinds of abuse.

285
00:22:51,800 --> 00:22:54,560
A lot of them get extorted
by corrupt police officers.

286
00:22:55,280 --> 00:22:58,120
Some have to pay thousands of baht
just to make it here for work.

287
00:22:58,760 --> 00:23:00,880
No one wants to be born
into a life of hardship.

288
00:23:01,400 --> 00:23:02,960
They just don't have a choice.

289
00:23:03,720 --> 00:23:04,800
I'm no different from them.

290
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:12,360
If I were a supervisor like you,

291
00:23:13,360 --> 00:23:15,640
I'd choose to protect my workers

292
00:23:15,720 --> 00:23:17,520
instead of criticizing me for what I did.

293
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:29,400
What are you doing?

294
00:23:29,480 --> 00:23:33,040
You're just a worker.
What right do you have to lecture me?

295
00:23:35,280 --> 00:23:38,200
You hate seeing people
get taken advantage of, right?

296
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:39,520
Then,

297
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:42,360
you shouldn't take advantage of anyone.

298
00:23:43,440 --> 00:23:44,360
Look over there.

299
00:23:48,840 --> 00:23:50,200
Get back to work.

300
00:23:54,760 --> 00:23:58,120
I was glad when you stepped in to help.

301
00:23:59,400 --> 00:24:01,280
I thought you were a good supervisor.

302
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:03,320
But now I know

303
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:05,960
you're not as good as I thought.

304
00:24:06,680 --> 00:24:10,400
You only helped because you wanted
to act tough in front of the police.

305
00:24:25,360 --> 00:24:28,040
Boss, you're seriously cold-blooded.

306
00:24:28,120 --> 00:24:29,640
That was brutal.

307
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:34,360
It has to be this way.

308
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:37,760
I'm following Mr. Pichai's orders.

309
00:24:39,480 --> 00:24:42,640
He wants me to test if this woman
really has the determination

310
00:24:43,560 --> 00:24:44,680
or if she's just all talk.

311
00:24:45,920 --> 00:24:48,080
My sweet, kind-hearted boss

312
00:24:48,160 --> 00:24:50,480
has turned into a maniac again.

313
00:24:58,560 --> 00:24:59,600
I got this.

314
00:25:09,080 --> 00:25:11,360
Everyone! That's it for today!

315
00:25:12,200 --> 00:25:14,960
Go on! See you tomorrow!

316
00:25:17,920 --> 00:25:19,480
Come on, everybody!

317
00:25:39,920 --> 00:25:41,840
Madam! Madam!

318
00:25:42,800 --> 00:25:43,640
Hey!

319
00:25:44,240 --> 00:25:47,040
Stop screaming! You're going
to burst my eardrums.

320
00:25:47,120 --> 00:25:47,960
What is it?

321
00:25:48,560 --> 00:25:52,040
Madam, that shameless woman's
daughter is back.

322
00:25:52,120 --> 00:25:52,960
Really?

323
00:25:53,680 --> 00:25:55,480
So? She's dead, right?

324
00:25:56,600 --> 00:25:59,000
She's not dead,
but she looks half-dead, ma'am.

325
00:26:01,040 --> 00:26:03,040
Then let's finish the job.

326
00:26:17,640 --> 00:26:18,480
Wait.

327
00:26:20,640 --> 00:26:23,120
Hello. I'm back.

328
00:26:24,720 --> 00:26:27,320
Look at you. Can you handle it?

329
00:26:27,840 --> 00:26:31,080
If you can't, I can give you
enough money for the trip home.

330
00:26:31,840 --> 00:26:33,000
I can handle it.

331
00:26:34,720 --> 00:26:37,280
I'll be going now.

332
00:26:39,520 --> 00:26:40,960
Where are you going?

333
00:26:41,560 --> 00:26:43,360
Back to my room to rest.

334
00:26:43,440 --> 00:26:47,640
Did you forget your place when Father

335
00:26:47,720 --> 00:26:49,120
let you stay in this house?

336
00:26:51,480 --> 00:26:55,360
There. Wash all those dishes
until they're spotless.

337
00:26:56,040 --> 00:26:57,440
When you're done, mop the floors.

338
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:00,920
Okay.

339
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:02,000
Oh.

340
00:27:02,680 --> 00:27:06,520
Goodness. You must be exhausted
after working so hard.

341
00:27:06,600 --> 00:27:09,640
I completely forgot to ask.
Have you eaten anything yet?

342
00:27:10,920 --> 00:27:12,240
Not yet.

343
00:27:13,920 --> 00:27:17,360
Well, I am your aunt by marriage.

344
00:27:17,440 --> 00:27:20,920
I wouldn't be so heartless
to my own family.

345
00:27:21,440 --> 00:27:23,160
- Chamoi
- Yes?

346
00:27:23,240 --> 00:27:25,160
saved some food for you.

347
00:27:26,320 --> 00:27:28,280
Thank you very much, Aunt Liu.

348
00:27:30,280 --> 00:27:31,600
- Chamoi.
- Yes?

349
00:27:32,240 --> 00:27:33,960
Bring my niece her food.

350
00:27:34,680 --> 00:27:35,800
Of course.

351
00:27:36,920 --> 00:27:40,080
Hurry up. My niece is hungry.

352
00:27:46,800 --> 00:27:49,200
Madam, I'm so sorry.
I don't know what happened.

353
00:27:49,280 --> 00:27:52,080
My hands suddenly went weak.

354
00:27:52,760 --> 00:27:54,280
What a mess.

355
00:27:54,960 --> 00:27:59,640
If you want anything to eat,
I guess you'll have to make it yourself.

356
00:27:59,720 --> 00:28:03,880
But you need to finish
all your work first.

357
00:28:03,960 --> 00:28:05,160
Then you can cook something.

358
00:28:13,960 --> 00:28:17,520
Oh, what a shame. Sorry. Looks like
you'll have to make your own food.

359
00:28:17,600 --> 00:28:21,680
But you have to finish
all your work first before you get to eat.

360
00:28:37,720 --> 00:28:40,440
Hathaya did everything
I told her to do today.

361
00:28:44,360 --> 00:28:46,200
<i>No matter how hard I pushed her,</i>

362
00:28:47,760 --> 00:28:50,880
<i>Hathaya never complained.
She didn't abandon the work either.</i>

363
00:28:51,560 --> 00:28:55,120
Also, one of our workers was extorted
by corrupt police officers today.

364
00:28:56,480 --> 00:28:58,560
Hathaya stepped in to protect him

365
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:01,120
without any fear.

366
00:29:06,080 --> 00:29:08,040
<i>She stood up for him completely.</i>

367
00:29:08,960 --> 00:29:10,320
<i>She wasn't afraid of them at all.</i>

368
00:29:12,120 --> 00:29:15,040
Then I warned her to be careful

369
00:29:15,120 --> 00:29:16,720
and not put herself in danger.

370
00:29:18,240 --> 00:29:19,360
But she wouldn't listen.

371
00:29:19,960 --> 00:29:22,600
She insisted on doing
what she believed was right.

372
00:29:22,680 --> 00:29:25,240
She trusted the evidence and the truth.

373
00:29:26,720 --> 00:29:28,520
And on top of that,

374
00:29:29,360 --> 00:29:31,760
she even criticized me
for trying to stop her.

375
00:29:32,440 --> 00:29:34,960
Exactly as I thought.

376
00:29:36,400 --> 00:29:39,920
She's stubborn and always
has to win, just like her mother.

377
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:42,240
No matter how good I tried to be,

378
00:29:42,320 --> 00:29:45,440
you never once opened
your heart to accept me.

379
00:29:45,520 --> 00:29:49,760
That's why you did everything you could

380
00:29:50,280 --> 00:29:52,480
to keep me away from Burapha.

381
00:29:54,720 --> 00:29:57,400
Her mother filled her head
with the same rotten ideas.

382
00:29:58,000 --> 00:29:59,200
Always blaming other people.

383
00:30:00,520 --> 00:30:03,960
What would you like me to do next, sir?

384
00:30:04,560 --> 00:30:07,040
Take Hathaya back
to the construction site.

385
00:30:08,280 --> 00:30:11,280
Make her do everything
the other laborers do.

386
00:30:15,320 --> 00:30:16,800
But I don't think

387
00:30:17,960 --> 00:30:20,040
Hathaya will be able to keep this up.

388
00:30:20,960 --> 00:30:22,720
It might be better to let her work

389
00:30:23,280 --> 00:30:24,800
in the office instead, sir.

390
00:30:25,920 --> 00:30:26,960
No.

391
00:30:28,560 --> 00:30:31,520
That woman is arrogant.

392
00:30:32,200 --> 00:30:35,040
I want to see how long she can last.

393
00:30:39,560 --> 00:30:40,560
Yes, sir.

394
00:30:53,720 --> 00:30:56,000
- Your food's ready.
- How much?

395
00:30:56,080 --> 00:30:57,160
One hundred baht.

396
00:30:57,240 --> 00:30:58,280
See you.

397
00:30:58,360 --> 00:30:59,760
- Thank you.
- Bye.

398
00:31:06,560 --> 00:31:10,480
Oh, Hathai. She still hasn't come back.

399
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:13,400
By now, she's probably
gambled all the money away.

400
00:31:15,120 --> 00:31:17,080
And if those debt collectors show up,

401
00:31:17,160 --> 00:31:19,080
where am I supposed
to find money to pay them?

402
00:31:25,560 --> 00:31:28,960
I don't have any money.
I really don't have any.

403
00:31:29,040 --> 00:31:30,640
Please don't hurt me.

404
00:31:30,720 --> 00:31:32,480
Mom. It's me.

405
00:31:34,320 --> 00:31:37,000
Hathai! That's not funny!

406
00:31:37,080 --> 00:31:38,480
You scared me half to death.

407
00:31:39,960 --> 00:31:40,880
Where's the money?

408
00:31:41,720 --> 00:31:44,520
You gambled it all away, didn't you?

409
00:31:44,600 --> 00:31:46,600
So now what are we going to do?

410
00:31:46,680 --> 00:31:48,720
Where are we supposed
to get money to pay the debt?

411
00:31:48,800 --> 00:31:50,240
- Mom.
- Let me see.

412
00:31:50,320 --> 00:31:51,760
- What?
- Let me see it!

413
00:31:51,840 --> 00:31:54,160
Mom! Don't worry.

414
00:31:54,240 --> 00:31:56,440
It's not even due yet.

415
00:31:56,520 --> 00:31:57,440
Listen.

416
00:31:58,200 --> 00:32:00,520
Then you need to hide
somewhere for a while.

417
00:32:00,600 --> 00:32:03,360
Otherwise, those people
are going to kill you.

418
00:32:03,440 --> 00:32:05,600
Why should I hide, Mom?

419
00:32:06,240 --> 00:32:07,600
Mom,

420
00:32:07,680 --> 00:32:09,840
if they show up,

421
00:32:13,080 --> 00:32:16,200
I'll smack them in the mouth
with this money.

422
00:32:19,560 --> 00:32:21,240
Where did you get that much money?

423
00:32:21,760 --> 00:32:22,920
Did you steal it?

424
00:32:23,920 --> 00:32:27,600
Keep your voice down.
Someone might hear you and rob us.

425
00:32:27,680 --> 00:32:29,560
Where did you get it?

426
00:32:29,640 --> 00:32:32,040
I took the money Hathaya gave me

427
00:32:32,120 --> 00:32:34,080
and invested it last night.

428
00:32:34,160 --> 00:32:38,120
I played cards all night and won
another 300,000, Mom.

429
00:32:38,200 --> 00:32:41,360
So now we've got 800,000.

430
00:32:44,160 --> 00:32:47,880
Good. Then go pay them right away
so this can finally be over.

431
00:32:48,680 --> 00:32:51,560
Why do I have to rush? It's not due yet.

432
00:32:52,200 --> 00:32:54,240
Just hurry up and pay it.

433
00:32:54,320 --> 00:32:56,200
Then your daughter won't
have to worry anymore.

434
00:32:56,280 --> 00:32:59,120
Mom. Just let me

435
00:32:59,200 --> 00:33:02,600
sleep with it and kiss it

436
00:33:02,680 --> 00:33:04,040
a little longer.

437
00:33:04,120 --> 00:33:07,120
I haven't seen this much money in ages.

438
00:33:09,320 --> 00:33:12,520
I played all night. I'm exhausted.

439
00:33:12,600 --> 00:33:14,040
I'm going to bed.

440
00:33:17,640 --> 00:33:21,640
Once the debt is paid off,
Hathaya can finally come home.

441
00:33:22,920 --> 00:33:24,640
Hang in there a little longer.

442
00:33:47,040 --> 00:33:49,320
Grandpa, don't come down yet!

443
00:33:49,400 --> 00:33:50,680
Why, sweetheart?

444
00:33:50,760 --> 00:33:54,600
Aunt Chamoi mopped the floor
but didn't dry it. You might slip.

445
00:34:03,840 --> 00:34:06,680
Hold onto the railing, Grandpa.
And come down slowly.

446
00:34:36,719 --> 00:34:38,679
You're safe now, Grandpa.

447
00:34:42,760 --> 00:34:45,080
Your knees are all red. Does it hurt?

448
00:34:46,040 --> 00:34:47,040
Yes.

449
00:34:47,120 --> 00:34:50,000
If your knees hurt, why are you
still wiping the floor?

450
00:34:50,080 --> 00:34:52,120
Because I'm worried about you, Grandpa.

451
00:34:54,239 --> 00:34:56,360
My beloved Hathaya.

452
00:34:56,440 --> 00:34:58,360
I love Grandpa more than anyone
in the world too.

453
00:34:58,440 --> 00:35:00,200
That makes Grandpa so happy.

454
00:35:11,360 --> 00:35:12,240
Grandpa,

455
00:35:13,080 --> 00:35:15,520
I've wiped the floor clean and dry.

456
00:35:15,600 --> 00:35:19,040
If you're coming down, please hold
onto the railing so you don't fall.

457
00:35:20,800 --> 00:35:22,360
I'm not some old, sick man

458
00:35:22,440 --> 00:35:24,960
who needs someone to take care of me.

459
00:35:25,880 --> 00:35:27,360
I can take care of myself.

460
00:35:29,600 --> 00:35:31,960
And don't think doing a few good deeds
is going to soften me.

461
00:35:33,760 --> 00:35:35,360
I'm not stupid enough

462
00:35:35,440 --> 00:35:37,440
to let anyone fool me that easily.

463
00:35:38,640 --> 00:35:39,600
Grandpa!

464
00:35:41,840 --> 00:35:42,880
Are you okay? Grandpa?

465
00:35:49,840 --> 00:35:51,320
Father!

466
00:35:53,960 --> 00:35:56,320
Father, are you all right?

467
00:35:57,040 --> 00:35:57,960
I'm fine.

468
00:35:58,040 --> 00:36:00,800
What did you do to Father?

469
00:36:02,040 --> 00:36:05,240
I didn't do anything. Grandpa
was about to fall, so I helped him.

470
00:36:05,320 --> 00:36:07,800
Father fell because of you.

471
00:36:12,040 --> 00:36:15,800
Good grief. Did you even attempt
to mop this? The floor is soaking wet.

472
00:36:15,880 --> 00:36:19,520
If Father had fallen down the stairs
and ended up disabled, what would you do?

473
00:36:22,560 --> 00:36:24,640
Or were you trying to hurt him?

474
00:36:25,440 --> 00:36:28,480
No. I wiped the floor completely dry.

475
00:36:28,560 --> 00:36:30,880
Check it if you don't believe me.
There's no water left.

476
00:36:38,240 --> 00:36:40,480
It really is wet! Oh, my goodness!

477
00:36:41,080 --> 00:36:43,480
Don't worry, sir.

478
00:36:43,560 --> 00:36:45,280
I'll wipe it completely dry for you.

479
00:36:45,800 --> 00:36:47,680
You always have an answer for everything.

480
00:36:48,200 --> 00:36:50,360
It's not time for you to go
to the construction site yet?

481
00:36:50,440 --> 00:36:53,640
Then go work in the kitchen.

482
00:37:07,080 --> 00:37:08,800
Father,

483
00:37:08,880 --> 00:37:11,760
you really have to be more careful.

484
00:37:12,320 --> 00:37:15,080
I don't trust Hathaya at all.

485
00:37:21,680 --> 00:37:23,560
What do you mean by that?

486
00:37:25,360 --> 00:37:28,840
I'm afraid Hathaya might try to hurt you.

487
00:37:31,640 --> 00:37:33,880
And please don't think
I'm trying to turn you against her.

488
00:37:33,960 --> 00:37:36,840
You know very well

489
00:37:36,920 --> 00:37:40,080
what Hathai did to us. She had an affair

490
00:37:40,160 --> 00:37:42,880
and humiliated you.

491
00:37:42,960 --> 00:37:46,480
Then she stole my jewelry
and all that money too.

492
00:37:47,400 --> 00:37:49,760
That was Hathai, not Hathaya.

493
00:37:50,880 --> 00:37:53,480
I understand. But her mother

494
00:37:53,560 --> 00:37:56,600
must have filled her head with ideas
about getting revenge on you.

495
00:37:57,240 --> 00:38:00,600
I don't trust her.
I'm afraid she might try to hurt you.

496
00:38:01,560 --> 00:38:04,240
Father, I think you should

497
00:38:04,320 --> 00:38:06,640
just throw some money at her
and get her out of here.

498
00:38:07,480 --> 00:38:09,280
Enough.

499
00:38:11,200 --> 00:38:14,680
I'm not stupid enough
to let anyone fool me again.

500
00:38:15,200 --> 00:38:16,720
And besides,

501
00:38:19,080 --> 00:38:22,560
I gave her my word.
I have to stand by what I said.

502
00:38:23,720 --> 00:38:26,440
Believe me. She won't last
until the end of the month.

503
00:38:27,720 --> 00:38:28,600
All right.

504
00:38:30,280 --> 00:38:32,080
Father, from now on,

505
00:38:32,160 --> 00:38:35,800
whenever you go up
or down the stairs, call me.

506
00:38:35,880 --> 00:38:38,640
Or call Chayanee to help you.

507
00:38:40,280 --> 00:38:41,320
Oh, right.

508
00:38:42,080 --> 00:38:45,720
Where is Chayanee?
I haven't seen her for several days.

509
00:38:48,680 --> 00:38:49,560
Oh, well...

510
00:38:49,640 --> 00:38:53,360
Chayanee said she went
on a trip with some old friends.

511
00:38:53,440 --> 00:38:55,480
She should be back in a day or two.

512
00:38:55,560 --> 00:38:59,040
But she video calls me every day.

513
00:38:59,120 --> 00:39:01,400
She keeps saying how much she misses you.

514
00:39:02,960 --> 00:39:05,840
When she gets back,
tell her to come see me.

515
00:39:06,360 --> 00:39:09,120
I want to ask her about the marketing plan
for the new development.

516
00:39:10,720 --> 00:39:11,600
Yes.

517
00:39:25,680 --> 00:39:27,640
I already told you, Mom.

518
00:39:27,720 --> 00:39:30,760
I want to be alone.
I just want some time to relax.

519
00:39:30,840 --> 00:39:33,520
Stop acting so carefree, Chayanee.

520
00:39:34,120 --> 00:39:36,720
That manipulative Hathaya
keeps hanging around Grandpa

521
00:39:36,800 --> 00:39:38,720
<i>and trying to please him.</i>

522
00:39:38,800 --> 00:39:41,320
Be careful. She's going to swoop in

523
00:39:41,400 --> 00:39:42,760
and steal your inheritance.

524
00:39:43,840 --> 00:39:45,320
Grandpa loves me.

525
00:39:45,400 --> 00:39:47,800
There's no way he'll give
any of the inheritance to her.

526
00:39:47,880 --> 00:39:49,560
Don't underestimate her.

527
00:39:49,640 --> 00:39:53,000
Old people need even more
attention and affection.

528
00:39:53,080 --> 00:39:54,640
You need to come back now.

529
00:39:54,720 --> 00:39:57,960
Grandpa asked about the marketing plan
for the housing development,

530
00:39:58,040 --> 00:39:59,160
and I had no answer.

531
00:40:00,040 --> 00:40:01,560
Okay. I know.

532
00:40:01,640 --> 00:40:02,760
You're awake?

533
00:40:04,440 --> 00:40:06,120
Chayanee, where are you?

534
00:40:06,200 --> 00:40:07,320
<i>Who are you with?</i>

535
00:40:07,400 --> 00:40:09,640
I'm with a friend. Talk later, Mom.

536
00:40:13,760 --> 00:40:14,600
Chayanee--

537
00:40:18,920 --> 00:40:19,760
Madam,

538
00:40:19,840 --> 00:40:23,080
there's no point calling her.
She won't answer anyway.

539
00:40:23,160 --> 00:40:24,480
Who is Chayanee with?

540
00:40:26,080 --> 00:40:26,920
Who is she with?

541
00:40:27,560 --> 00:40:30,080
That's what I'm asking! Who is she with?

542
00:40:30,640 --> 00:40:31,640
I heard a man's voice.

543
00:40:31,720 --> 00:40:32,800
A man?!

544
00:40:34,080 --> 00:40:34,920
‎Her husband!

545
00:40:35,000 --> 00:40:36,080
You idiot!

546
00:40:36,160 --> 00:40:39,200
She's still single. She doesn't
even have a boyfriend, let alone husband.

547
00:40:39,280 --> 00:40:41,000
You never know these days, madam.

548
00:40:41,080 --> 00:40:43,440
Women today just don't care
what anyone thinks.

549
00:40:44,080 --> 00:40:46,760
You really have a foul mouth.

550
00:40:47,640 --> 00:40:49,760
- Go! Get out!
- Yes, ma'am!

551
00:40:58,000 --> 00:40:59,560
Smells so good.

552
00:41:00,520 --> 00:41:03,040
Do you mean the coffee or me?

553
00:41:05,640 --> 00:41:08,360
The coffee smells good,
but you smell even better.

554
00:41:10,680 --> 00:41:11,800
Raiwin,

555
00:41:11,880 --> 00:41:15,680
how much longer are you going
to keep our relationship a secret?

556
00:41:17,680 --> 00:41:20,840
Right now, Dad wants me to focus on work.

557
00:41:20,920 --> 00:41:23,440
And he wants me to run
in the next election too.

558
00:41:24,280 --> 00:41:26,080
I don't think we can go public yet.

559
00:41:30,280 --> 00:41:31,920
You're not a child anymore.

560
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:34,360
You need to have a mind of your own.

561
00:41:35,520 --> 00:41:39,400
Do you know how much
the world has changed?

562
00:41:40,480 --> 00:41:44,200
If you let your girlfriend
help you campaign,

563
00:41:44,280 --> 00:41:46,360
you could win support
from younger voters too.

564
00:41:49,800 --> 00:41:52,040
I really did choose the right woman.

565
00:41:52,800 --> 00:41:54,720
All right.

566
00:41:54,800 --> 00:41:57,640
I'll talk to my father today. Okay?

567
00:41:58,240 --> 00:41:59,560
Okay.

568
00:42:13,400 --> 00:42:14,600
Ramil,

569
00:42:14,680 --> 00:42:17,080
have breakfast with me.
I prepared delicious food for you.

570
00:42:18,960 --> 00:42:21,320
Mom, you usually have me eat
at roadside stalls.

571
00:42:22,280 --> 00:42:25,440
What's special about today?
Why did you invite me to the main house?

572
00:42:26,640 --> 00:42:28,320
We haven't eaten together in a long time.

573
00:42:28,400 --> 00:42:30,400
I just want to have a meal with you, okay?

574
00:42:30,480 --> 00:42:31,440
Come on.

575
00:42:32,720 --> 00:42:34,400
Come with me.

576
00:42:42,800 --> 00:42:44,640
Were you never taught manners?

577
00:42:45,680 --> 00:42:47,520
Why do you make your elders wait for you?

578
00:42:48,360 --> 00:42:51,120
Didn't your father
ever teach you any manners?

579
00:42:53,040 --> 00:42:55,720
Ramil, come eat with us.

580
00:42:56,440 --> 00:42:57,600
Go sit down, sweetheart.

581
00:43:06,520 --> 00:43:09,520
I really don't want to sit
at the same table with you.

582
00:43:11,640 --> 00:43:14,400
But today it's necessary.
I have something to discuss with you.

583
00:43:16,360 --> 00:43:20,400
I want you to resign
from Mr. Pichai's company

584
00:43:21,040 --> 00:43:22,880
and start a new company.

585
00:43:23,880 --> 00:43:26,680
You've worked with Mr. Pichai
for a long time.

586
00:43:26,760 --> 00:43:28,400
You should know the system

587
00:43:28,480 --> 00:43:32,400
and have connections
with suppliers and labor brokers.

588
00:43:33,960 --> 00:43:37,160
I want you to become your own boss.

589
00:43:37,680 --> 00:43:39,720
Stop working for someone else.

590
00:43:39,800 --> 00:43:41,680
Everything I'm saying

591
00:43:42,360 --> 00:43:44,600
is for your own benefit.

592
00:43:46,480 --> 00:43:47,880
Thank Mr. Saksit, sweetheart.

593
00:43:54,880 --> 00:43:56,120
Why me?

594
00:43:57,520 --> 00:44:00,280
Why not have Raiwin,
your own biological son, do it?

595
00:44:00,360 --> 00:44:03,640
Raiwin is going to run
for Subdistrict Chief in my place.

596
00:44:03,720 --> 00:44:06,720
As for you, you're not my son.

597
00:44:07,960 --> 00:44:10,120
So you need to set up the company

598
00:44:10,200 --> 00:44:12,200
and act as my nominee.

599
00:44:12,280 --> 00:44:14,280
Then we can take contracts
from local government.

600
00:44:14,880 --> 00:44:16,080
What do I get?

601
00:44:18,440 --> 00:44:20,840
Someone like you gets a regular salary.

602
00:44:21,480 --> 00:44:25,480
And you'll receive 20%

603
00:44:25,560 --> 00:44:26,880
of the company's annual profit.

604
00:44:27,800 --> 00:44:28,640
I won't do it.

605
00:44:29,880 --> 00:44:30,920
Why?

606
00:44:31,000 --> 00:44:33,840
You want more? I'll give you 30%.

607
00:44:33,920 --> 00:44:35,160
I said I won't do it.

608
00:44:36,720 --> 00:44:38,480
You dare disobey me?

609
00:44:38,560 --> 00:44:40,840
Even if you gave me 100%,

610
00:44:42,440 --> 00:44:43,400
I still wouldn't do it.

611
00:44:44,360 --> 00:44:46,480
How dare you defy me!

612
00:44:46,560 --> 00:44:48,480
First of all,

613
00:44:49,440 --> 00:44:53,040
Mr. Pichai gave me
an opportunity when I graduated.

614
00:44:53,560 --> 00:44:55,240
I will not betray him.

615
00:44:56,000 --> 00:44:58,440
And most importantly,

616
00:44:59,040 --> 00:45:02,240
I refuse to set up a nominee company
to take public contracts.

617
00:45:03,320 --> 00:45:04,960
This country

618
00:45:05,040 --> 00:45:08,040
has already suffered enough
because of corruption.

619
00:45:08,920 --> 00:45:12,360
I will never serve a corrupt politician.

620
00:45:16,000 --> 00:45:16,840
Ramil!

621
00:45:18,040 --> 00:45:20,360
Know your place.

622
00:45:20,960 --> 00:45:23,120
Everything you've had since childhood

623
00:45:23,200 --> 00:45:25,280
is because of me!

624
00:45:25,880 --> 00:45:27,640
If I hadn't taken care of you,

625
00:45:28,160 --> 00:45:29,920
you'd probably be a beggar by now.

626
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:33,240
Or a drug runner
or some junkie living on the streets.

627
00:45:33,320 --> 00:45:36,080
Show some gratitude
for what I've done for you,

628
00:45:36,160 --> 00:45:37,520
parasite!

629
00:45:42,240 --> 00:45:43,120
Ramil!

630
00:45:45,880 --> 00:45:47,160
Why are you still here?

631
00:45:47,800 --> 00:45:51,680
Make your son apologize to me.
Make him remember everything he owes me.

632
00:45:51,760 --> 00:45:53,960
Bring him here
and make him kneel before me!

633
00:45:54,040 --> 00:45:55,760
I'm sorry on Ramil's behalf.

634
00:45:55,840 --> 00:45:58,560
Go! Bring him back
and make him apologize. Go!

635
00:46:00,280 --> 00:46:01,480
Damn it.

636
00:46:03,920 --> 00:46:07,000
- Dad, I need to talk to you.
- No more talking.

637
00:46:07,080 --> 00:46:08,640
And I'm not eating either!

638
00:46:14,560 --> 00:46:17,040
Ramil! Ramil!

639
00:46:18,520 --> 00:46:22,000
What Mr. Saksit did was because
he wants what's best for you.

640
00:46:22,520 --> 00:46:25,320
We're all family.
We have to help each other.

641
00:46:25,400 --> 00:46:27,720
If he really considered me
part of this family,

642
00:46:28,560 --> 00:46:29,760
why can't I live here then?

643
00:46:31,920 --> 00:46:33,880
It's been over ten years

644
00:46:35,040 --> 00:46:36,880
since you divorced Dad

645
00:46:37,400 --> 00:46:38,840
and brought me here.

646
00:46:39,360 --> 00:46:42,560
Not once have I ever felt
that he treated you

647
00:46:42,640 --> 00:46:44,640
with the respect a wife deserves.

648
00:46:45,160 --> 00:46:46,920
He just wanted someone to run the house,

649
00:46:47,600 --> 00:46:49,560
manage the servants,

650
00:46:50,480 --> 00:46:54,400
and raise Raiwin after his mother died.

651
00:46:55,680 --> 00:46:59,000
I'm not even sure he ever loved you.

652
00:46:59,080 --> 00:47:00,440
Maybe he just wanted a servant!

653
00:47:01,840 --> 00:47:02,920
Don't ever say that again.

654
00:47:05,880 --> 00:47:07,760
If Mr. Saksit hadn't helped us,

655
00:47:07,840 --> 00:47:10,720
where would we be living now?
What kind of life would we have?

656
00:47:11,440 --> 00:47:15,440
I've never forgotten
that he helped us. But Mom,

657
00:47:16,520 --> 00:47:18,400
we've served him long enough.

658
00:47:23,720 --> 00:47:26,280
Mom, I'm grown now.

659
00:47:27,640 --> 00:47:29,120
I can take care of you.

660
00:47:30,600 --> 00:47:32,160
Come live with me.

661
00:47:33,600 --> 00:47:34,440
Please, Mom.

662
00:47:40,840 --> 00:47:42,520
I can't be ungrateful to him.

663
00:47:50,840 --> 00:47:52,320
I don't understand, Mom.

664
00:47:53,120 --> 00:47:56,240
Why do you keep giving in to him?
Why put up with living like this?!

665
00:48:00,320 --> 00:48:02,200
If you don't want to start the company,

666
00:48:02,720 --> 00:48:04,960
I respect your decision.

667
00:48:06,560 --> 00:48:08,960
But I want you to apologize to Mr. Saksit.

668
00:48:10,840 --> 00:48:12,560
If I'm wrong, I'll apologize.

669
00:48:14,400 --> 00:48:16,440
But I will never bow my head

670
00:48:16,960 --> 00:48:18,880
to someone who intends to steal.

671
00:48:36,800 --> 00:48:39,240
Make it even.

672
00:48:40,920 --> 00:48:42,800
Is something bothering you?

673
00:48:43,320 --> 00:48:45,480
If something's troubling you,
you can tell me.

674
00:48:51,040 --> 00:48:53,520
I'm not trying to interfere
in your business.

675
00:48:54,400 --> 00:48:57,720
I just don't want the workers
to have to deal with your bad mood.

676
00:49:05,400 --> 00:49:06,600
Keep it up!

677
00:49:07,320 --> 00:49:08,440
You too!

678
00:49:13,240 --> 00:49:14,080
Hey, boss.

679
00:49:14,160 --> 00:49:18,040
I heard your mom invited you
to eat at the main house.

680
00:49:18,120 --> 00:49:19,240
Was the food good?

681
00:49:28,800 --> 00:49:30,600
Why are you standing there?

682
00:49:30,680 --> 00:49:32,640
Don't you have work to do?
Get back to work!

683
00:49:34,800 --> 00:49:36,520
You guys are in for a rough day.

684
00:49:46,160 --> 00:49:47,480
I started with 500,000

685
00:49:47,560 --> 00:49:50,080
and made 300,000 in just one night.

686
00:49:51,400 --> 00:49:54,200
If I take all 800,000 and play again,

687
00:49:54,720 --> 00:49:57,000
wouldn't I come back
with more than a million?

688
00:50:13,920 --> 00:50:16,480
Every time you call,
it's always about some mess,

689
00:50:16,560 --> 00:50:18,080
<i>some problem I have to fix.</i>

690
00:50:18,160 --> 00:50:20,200
<i>You're selfish. How dare you</i>

691
00:50:20,280 --> 00:50:21,040
‎NEXT EPISODE

692
00:50:21,120 --> 00:50:22,720
tell other people about my business?

693
00:50:22,800 --> 00:50:25,200
- You're talking about your father.
- None of your business.

694
00:50:25,280 --> 00:50:28,000
Hot rice porridge is ready.

695
00:50:28,080 --> 00:50:30,800
The kitchen staff said
Hathaya woke up late.

696
00:50:30,880 --> 00:50:32,760
<i>I was worried about you, Grandpa,</i>

697
00:50:32,840 --> 00:50:35,800
<i>so I made you some rice porridge
and prepared your medicine.</i>

698
00:50:35,880 --> 00:50:37,520
<i>As Subdistrict Chief here,</i>

699
00:50:37,600 --> 00:50:40,080
<i>when we move out,
we will definitely have a place to live.</i>

700
00:50:40,160 --> 00:50:41,200
<i>No way!</i>

701
00:50:41,280 --> 00:50:44,480
What were you thinking,
risking your own life for them?!

702
00:51:40,560 --> 00:51:42,840
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
